# Prettier reads .gitignore too. A slash starts each pattern, which names a path from the root: without it a name matches at any
# depth, and `documentation` also left scripts/documentation/ unformatted
# What the tools write: the executable, the importer's candles, the coverage reports, Bun's lockfile
/dist
/db
/coverage
/bun.lock
# The guides, whose tables are aligned by hand
/documentation
# semantic-release writes it: its notes stay as the generator wrote them, as on the GitHub release
/CHANGELOG.md
# The worktrees the Claude desktop app checks out under .claude/worktrees/: copies of the checkout, whose guides the anchored
# /documentation above does not reach, hidden from git by .git/info/exclude, which Prettier does not read
/.claude
